\node at (3.45, 0) {$\scriptstyle d_2$};
}
\end{equation}
where we connect the edge in the image of $A_e$ to show that the 1-skeleton has been condensed. 
We now define the projection $B_f$ for $f \in F(\Gamma)$. 
The projection $B_f$ acts on $\prod_{e \in f} A_e \cH_f$. 
Here, we write $e \in f$ to denote that the edge $e$ is adjacent to the face $f$, and we have $\cH_f \coloneqq \bigotimes_{v \in f} \cH_v$, where $v \in f$ means that $v$ is adjacent to an edge adjacent to $f$. 
Specifically, $B_f$ acts on simple tensors as follows: 
\begin{equation}
B_f
\left( \tikzmath{
